					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaguelydownwards" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5552255); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5552255&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200768" alt="VaguelyDownwards" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5552255)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaguelydownwards" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5552255); return false;" >VaguelyDownwards</a></span> <span class="odate time_1565974606 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Aug 2019 16:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4332358">
									

<p>Some good bones, but feels like it still needs a few rounds of polishing. What stands out to me is the inconsistent Hulk Speech from &quot;Subject&quot; and the emphasis on IQ. IQ scores and the ability to form a coherent sentence are two different things, and it's especially weird to see it switch from &quot;I no remember&quot; to &quot;I know that my blood grows the fungus.&quot;</p>
<p>Do you have a definite answer for how much the Subject understands about their condition? How much awareness they have left? Do they have a concept of lying? Of free will? Do they consider themselves an individual who serves the fungus, the fungus itself, something else? Is the fungus sapient separately from the host? You don't have to reveal all the answers in the article, and often less is more, but it'll help you write if you know the answers.</p>

							</div>

								
					
