														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4618673">
									

<p>Short and sweet SCP, I enjoyed it.</p>
<p>I'd advise going over the interview log again, though. Making the subject appear actually stupid is gonna be way harder than it's worth, I think. &quot;I no remember&quot; speech cringed me out a little bit, as well as &quot;Hello, Subject.&quot; I'd advise replacing Subject with [DATA EXPUNGED] to imply that the interviewer used the person's previous identity. as well as &quot;formerly known as [REDACTED]&quot; to &quot;formerly [DATA EXPUNGED]&quot;. This implies that the identity was wiped off the record entirely. Or, it might even be a better idea to make up a name like Karliah Jones and replace that same number of characters with full block icons. Up to you.</p>
<p>Hell, I'd remove the whole IQ lowering thing overall and make the person behave as if they're normal but memory-wiped and suddenly outside the control of their actions. I think that'd be scarier, anyways.</p>
<p>Also, as another commenter said, removing the spleen, in particular, seems a bit unnecessary. Writing &quot;yo, if you find a -2, chuck his ass in the incinerator&quot; in a clinical tone is a perfectly acceptable containment measure.</p>

							</div>

								
					
